{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>And moreover, what are you to me</b> — He prophesies concerning Tyre and Sidon and Philistia, that the day of their disaster shall come. Now we find it written that the Philistines would bring tribute and silver as tribute to Jehoshaphat, and this is a sign that his hand prevailed over them." "<b>And the meaning of recompense</b> — as though I recompensed you evil, or you are the ones who begin to recompense me, as in: \"whom we recompensed\"."], :book :joel, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Joel -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/yoel"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:06:41.506693527Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}